{
	"_comment": [
		"Hoenn's map as a vote graph. Hand-curated, not generated: the decomp's warp",
		"tables are exhaustive and noisy (every door, every ledge, every one-way drop),",
		"and what this needs is the shape of a playthrough, not the shape of the ROM.",
		"",
		"Connections are declared in both directions and validated on load.",
		"'requires' gates travel INTO a location; 'gymRequires' gates the gym only.",
		"Routes split into north/south halves where a interior sits between them,",
		"because that is how you actually traverse them.",
		"",
		"trainers[] and encounters are filled in by later milestones; the ids here",
		"are the keys those tables will be looked up by."
	],

